title: Overview
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

The Usage section explains how to organize fieldwork and manage the records
that make up a NAHPU project. Use these pages as a reference while setting up
a project, collecting data, and transferring or exporting it.

## Usage topics

- [Device Requirements](./devices): Choose field devices and accessories based
  on your field conditions, budget, and access to electricity.
- [Projects](./projects): Create projects and configure project information,
  settings, and time zones.
- [Settings](./settings): Configure catalog formats, field IDs, controlled
  vocabularies, database records, export presets, theme, and data usage.
- [Personnel](./personnel): Manage people in the database and assign them to
  projects and fieldwork roles.
- [Sites](./sites): Record field locations, coordinates, and site information.
- [Collecting Events](./events): Record the activities, effort, personnel,
  weather, and astronomy associated with fieldwork.
- [Specimens](./specimens): Create and manage specimen records, capture data,
  identifications, preservation, and media.
- [Taxon](./taxon): Manage taxonomic names and import or export taxon lists.
- [Narrative](./narrative): Keep a field journal for observations and context
  that does not fit in another record type.
- [Export](./export): Back up, transfer, and export project data and documents.
